      "t": "p",
      "x": "From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted into [[A]] through [[C]] in the program."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "The procedure `reverse_digits` receives one positive integer argument named `num` and outputs both the original integer and the integer with its digits reversed. Assume that the ones digit of `num` is not 0."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "x": "Number is 456, output 654\nNumber is 23407, output 70432"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "[Program]"
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "x": "○ reverse_digits(integer: num)\n  integer: rev ← 0\n  integer: rm ← 0\n  integer: temp ← num\n  while ([[A]])\n    rm ← temp mod 10\n    rev ← [[B]]\n    temp ← [[C]]\n  endwhile\n  output \"Number is \", num, \", output \", rev"
    },
